{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: implement `solve(case)` that filters API calls based on the Toolformer-style filtering mechanism.\n\nFrom the candidate_artifact description:\n1. For each call: gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n2. Normalize gain by prediction_tokens: normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n3. Accept a call if: parseable == True AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Keep diagnostics in supplied call order\n5. Return accepted_call_ids and per-call diagnostics\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: loss_without=1.48911432, loss_with=0.30132987, tokens=5, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445\n  - normalized_gain = 1.18778445 / 5 = 0.23755689\n  - parseable=true, 0.23755689 \u003e= 0.05 → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.37006381 - 0.10127803 = 1.26878578, norm = 1.26878578/5 = 0.25375716, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.07992348 - 0.04054692 = 1.03937656, norm = 1.03937656/5 = 0.20787531, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.76582941 - 0.57732788 = 1.18850153, norm = 1.18850153/3 = 0.39616718, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.70674574 - 0.40289862 = 1.30384712, norm = 1.30384712/6 = 0.21730785, parseable=true → accepted\n- call5: parseable=false → rejected\n\nThe description says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I'll round normalized_gain to some reasonable precision. Let me check what \"rounded\" means here - probably round to some decimal places. I'll use round(..., 8) or similar to keep precision but handle floating point.\n\nActually, looking at the schema, normalized_gain is just \"number\" type. Let me use round to maybe 8 decimal places to avoid floating point issues, but not lose precision.\n\nNow let me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        normalized_gain = round(normalized_gain, 8)\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me also add validation for required fields as mentioned in the artifact (\"Validate every required field before computing a result\").\n\nThe output should be a JSON object with `implementation` key containing the Python source as a string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate top-level required fields\\n    required_top = [\\\"threshold\\\", \\\"calls\\\"]\\n    for key in required_top:\\n        if key not in case:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required field: {key}\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"'calls' must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    required_call_fields = [\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        for field in required_call_fields:\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Call missing required field '{field}': {call}\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, (int, float)) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call '{call_id}'\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n        normalized_gain = round(normalized_gain, 8)\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_015d8PEhOC4vKV4fuI2glQcq","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2446},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2446,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":66,"output_tokens":1385,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":908},"service_tier":"standard"}}